Id: osv002f
Severity: FAIL
Category: packages
Check: check_release
Fix: Upgrade to a release the distribution still supports (do-release-upgrade, dnf system-upgrade, or the release notes' upgrade steps), or buy its extended support.
References: os-release(5); https://endoflife.date
Controls: CIS 2.2; NIST SA-22; ISO 8.8; CE Security update management

The installed release of the distribution is past the end of its
security support: holes found since that date are fixed in the
releases still supported, not in this one, and its package manager
offers no updates for them. The release comes from /etc/os-release
(the image's, under --root) and the date from the table Tigris
carries, systems/Linux/2/eol_list, made from endoflife.date by
util/mkeol for every Tigris release; an audit never goes to the
network for it.

Where the distribution sells extended support (RHEL, Ubuntu Pro's
ESM, SUSE, Freexian's ELTS for Debian), the detail says until when; a
system that has it can accept this finding with tigris-accept until
that date.
